---
title: API reference
---

Import types from `@logit/core` for editor help. These are the shapes as of the
current release.

## Manifest

```ts
type PluginManifest = {
  id: string;
  family: "exercise-pack" | "progression-algorithm" | "mobility-progression"
        | "mobility-pack" | "muscle-group-insight" | "analytics"
        | "nutrition-algorithm" | "nutrition-analytics" | "widget";
  name: string;
  description: string;
  version: string;                 // semver, bump every change
  author?: string;
  integrity?: string;              // sha256-<base64> of the artifact — required to publish
  minAppVersion?: string;
  homepageUrl?: string;
  distribution:
    | { origin: "url"; manifestUrl: string; bundleUrl: string }
    | { origin: "inline"; data: unknown };   // exercise-pack only
  capabilities: Array<{ family: string /* = manifest.family */; [idField]: string /* = manifest.id */ }>;
};
```

Capability id field by family: `exercisePackId`, `mobilityPackId`, `algorithmId`
(progression, mobility-progression, muscle-group-insight & nutrition),
`analyticsId` (analytics & nutrition-analytics), `widgetId`.

## Bundle descriptor

Every code bundle exports this:

```ts
export const pluginBundle = {
  formatVersion: 1,
  pluginId: string,                // = manifest.id
  family: string,                  // = manifest.family
  entryExport: string,             // name of the export below, e.g. "algorithm"
} as const;
```

A bundle is **one file, no `import` statements** — build with
`esbuild --bundle --format=esm`.

## Entry exports

| Family | Export shape |
|---|---|
| `progression-algorithm` | `{ id, name, description, defaultState, defaultPreferences?, preferencesSchema?, suggest(input) }` |
| `mobility-progression` | `{ id, name, description, defaultState, defaultPreferences?, preferencesSchema?, suggest(input) }` |
| `muscle-group-insight` | `{ id, name, description, defaultState, defaultPreferences?, preferencesSchema?, analyze(input) }` |
| `analytics` | `{ id, name, description, metricDefinitions, compute(input) }` |
| `nutrition-algorithm` | `{ id, name, description, defaultPreferences?, preferencesSchema?, computeTargets(input) }` |
| `nutrition-analytics` | `{ id, name, description, metricDefinitions, compute(input) }` |
| `widget` | `{ id, name, description, needs: string[], compute(input) }` |

## Input / output types

- **Progression** — `@logit/core/domain/progression`: `ProgressionInput`, `ProgressionOutput`
- **Mobility progression** — `@logit/core/domain/mobilityProgression`: `MobilityProgressionInput`, `MobilityProgressionOutput`
- **Muscle group insight** — `@logit/core/domain/muscleGroupInsight`: `MuscleGroupInsightInput`, `MuscleGroupInsightOutput`
- **Analytics** — `@logit/core/domain/analytics`: `AnalyticsInput`, `AnalyticsOutput`
- **Nutrition algorithm** — `@logit/core/domain/nutritionAlgorithm`
- **Nutrition analytics** — `@logit/core/domain/nutritionAnalytics`
- **Widget** — `@logit/core/plugins/widgetView`: `WidgetInput`, `WidgetView`, `WidgetNode`, `WidgetAction`
- **Reasoning** — `@logit/core/domain/reasoning`: `Reasoning`, `ReasoningConfidence` — the optional
  "show your work" shape a progression algorithm can attach (required for muscle group insight);
  see [progression algorithms](/docs/plugins/progression#reasoning-and-nudges).

## Sandbox limits

- ~300 ms wall-clock deadline per call
- 32 MB memory
- no DOM / `fetch` / storage / timers
- fresh VM per call — persist nothing in module scope
- input and output must be JSON-serialisable
